flsetup -- first boot: choose the keyboard
==========================================

Started by `flcomp --firstboot` when /etc/keyboard.conf is missing. Four
layouts (QWERTZ German, QWERTY US, QWERTY UK, AZERTY French), a preview of
the keys and a field to try them in (it uses the chosen layout at once, not
the compositor's). Continue writes `LAYOUT=de` (de, us, uk, fr) to
/etc/keyboard.conf and exits 0; exit 1 if the window was closed unsaved.

FL_KEYBOARD_CONF=FILE overrides the path (tests). FLUI_PPM=out.ppm renders
the window without a compositor.

Build: make; make install (PREFIX, DESTDIR). Needs libflui.
